-- Freshservice: tickets and requesters of your service desk
--
-- Creates a database read from your Freshservice account through the official API (v2, read only):
--   • Requesters: name, email, phones, job title, active;
--   • Tickets: subject, requester (linked), agent and group (names), status, priority, urgency, impact,
--     source, type, category, due dates, tags, description and a link to the ticket in Freshservice;
--   • a report “Open tickets”: overview, by requester, by group, requester × group.
--
-- Access: your Freshservice domain (“yourcompany” for yourcompany.freshservice.com) and your API key
-- (Freshservice › your profile › Profile settings › API key). The key is kept in the Keychain of this
-- device, never in the database; leave the fields empty on the next runs.
--
-- Which tickets: those updated during the last months (12 by default), the predefined Freshservice
-- filters (“New and my open”, “Watching”), or your own filter query, in the Freshservice syntax:
-- status:2 AND priority:4, agent_id:null, tag:'vpn'… (status: 2 Open, 3 Pending, 4 Resolved,
-- 5 Closed; priority: 1 Low to 4 Urgent). The database adds its own collections: open, pending,
-- urgent, overdue, unassigned, resolved…
--
-- To bring the database up to date later, run the action “Refresh from Freshservice” (Scripts entry of
-- the sidebar, or the database menu): it reads Freshservice again with the same choice of tickets and
-- updates the records in place, keeping your own fields and records. “Refresh this ticket” (menu of a
-- ticket) reads one ticket again, with its full description.

